{"id":"word:hebrew:H4994","type":"word","title":"נָא","subtitle":"H4994 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"'I pray' , 'now' , or 'then' ; added mostly to verbs (in the Imperative or Future), or to interjections, occasionally to an adverb or conjunction","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to נָא (H4994) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: inj.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 403 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"נָא (nâʼ) means 'I pray' , 'now' , or 'then' ; added mostly to verbs (in the Imperative or Future), or to interjections, occasionally to an adverb or conjunction First listed occurrence: 1Chr 21 8."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"נָא","transliteration":"nâʼ","pronunciation":"naw","strong":"H4994","lemmaId":"hebrew:H4994","partOfSpeech":"inj","forms":["נָ֣א","נָ֥א","נָא֙","נָ֤א","נָ֖א"],"morphs":[["HTe",332],["HTj",71]]},"definitions":{"short":"'I pray' , 'now' , or 'then' ; added mostly to verbs (in the Imperative or Future), or to interjections, occasionally to an adverb or conjunction","usage":"I beseech (pray) thee (you), go to, now, oh.","full":"H4994. na I. נָא particle of entreaty or exhortation I (we) pray, now (enclitic) (Syriac , ; compare Ethiopic veni, age! Di § 160. 1 Lex:675 Kö ii. 244 ); — attached: 1 to the imperative, especially in colloquial style , when it expresses an entreaty or admonition, as Gen 12:13 אִמְרִינָֿא say, I pray , 13:9 הִמָּרֶדֿ מֵעָלַי נָא , 13:14 עֵינֶיךָ שָׂאנָֿא , 15:5 השׁמימה הַבֶּטנָֿא , 24:2 + often, Num 20:10 המוֺרים שׁמעונֿא , Judg 13:4 ; 16:6 , 10 , 28 ; 18:5 , etc., Isa 1:18 ; 5:3 ; Amos 7:2 , 5 ; rarely in a command, Gen 22:2 ; Isa 7:3 ). Ironically, in a challenge, 47:12 ; Job 40:10 . Once anomalously attached to a substantive, or (accents) prefixed to a verb, Num 12:13 נָא֖ רְָפא נָא֛ אֵ֕ל (Ew § 246 a Di אַלנָֿא ; see 3b ). 2 to the perfect with waw consecutive, in a precative sense (Dr § 119 δ ) Gen 40:14 . 3 to the imperfect, when leave is asked , or a prayer or desire expressed; a. in 1 person, especially with ה cohortative, Gen 19:8 אוציאהנֿא let me, I pray , bring out, 19:20 שָׁ֑מָּה אִמָּֽלְטָהנָּֿא , 24:12 לְפָנַי הַקְרֵהנָֿא 24:14 הַטִּינָֿא 24:17 ; 24:23 ; 24:43 ; 24:45 ; 25:30 ; 32:12 , 30 + often, Exod 3:18 נלכהנֿא let us go, I pray , Num 20:17 ; Isa 5:5 ; and in self-deliberation, Gen 18:21 ארדהנּֿא I will go down, now ! Exod 3:3 ואראה אסורהנּֿא I will turn aside, now , and see, 2Sam 14:15 ; Song 3:2 ; Isa 5:1 ; with אַל Job 32:21 . b. in 2 person, with אַל , in deprecation, Gen 18:3 עבדך מעל תעבר אלנֿא , 19:7 ; 47:29 ; Num 10:31 , etc.; hence elliptical אלנֿא do not, I pray , (do this,) Gen 19:18 ; 33:10 ; Num 12:13 Ew Di. c. in 3 person , Gen 18:4 יֻקַּחנָֿא let there be brought, I pray , 26:28 ; 33:14 ; 44:18 , 33 , etc., 2Sam 14:11-12 , 17 ; 1Kin 17:21 ; 2Kin 2:9 ; Psa 7:10 ; 118:2 ; 118:3 ; ironically Isa 19:12 ; 47:13 , or defiantly Jer 17:15 where is the word of J.? נָא יָבוֺא ; with אַל , Gen 13:8 מְרִיבָה תְהִי אַלנָֿא , 18:30 לַאדֹנָי יִחַר אַלנָֿא , 37:27 ; Num 12:12 . 4 joined to conjunctions and interjections: a. [ אָהּנָֿא , contracted] אָ֫נָּא . b. אַלנָֿא see above 3b, c. c. אִםנָֿא , especially in the phrase בעיניך חן מצאתי נא אם , used by one craving a favourable hearing Gen 30:27 ; 33:10 ; Judg 6:17 ; 1Sam 27:5 , and with נא repeated in the request itself Gen 18:3 ; 47:29 ; 50:4 ; Exod 33:13 ; 34:9 ; otherwise Gen 24:42 . d. הִנֵּהנָֿא behold, I pray , craving a favourable consideration of the fact pointed to by הִנֵּה , and of the request founded upon it (with which נא is often repeated), Gen 12:11 ; 16:2 ; 18:27 , 31 ; 19:2 , 8 , 19 , 20 ; 27:2 ; Judg 13:3 ; 19:9 ; 1Sam 9:6 ; 16:15 ; 2Sam 13:24 ; 2Kin 2:16 , 19 ; 4:9 +, Job 13:18 ; 33:2 ; 40:15-16 ,. e. ( לנו ) לי אוֺינָֿא Woe, now , to me (us) ! Jer 4:31 ; 45:3 ; Lam 5:16 . f. אַיֵּהנָֿא where, pray ? Psa 115:2 . g. נֶגְדָּהנָּֿא , peculiarly, Psa 116:14 ; 116:18 my vows to J. I will perform, לכלעֿמו נגדהנֿא O that (it may be) before all his people ! II. נָא adjective see ניא . II. נָא adjective raw , of flesh Exod 12:9 (P; opposed to בשׁל ). I. נָא [ נִיב ], נֵיבָ֑י נִיבָ֑י, see נוב . נִיד v . נוד . נִירָה see II. נדד . נָיוֺת see נוית below I. נוה . נִיתוֺתַ נִיחֹחַ, see נוח . נִין see נון .","rootNote":"a primitive particle of incitement and entreaty, which may usually be rendered;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 21 8","keyReferences":["1Chr 21 8","1Chr 21 13","1Chr 21 17","1Chr 22 5","1Chr 29 20","1Kgs 1 12","1Kgs 2 17","1Kgs 8 26"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":403,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 21 8","book":"1Chr","chapter":21,"verse":8,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נָא֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTe"},{"reference":"1Chr 21 13","book":"1Chr","chapter":21,"verse":13,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נָּ֣א","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTj"},{"reference":"1Chr 21 17","book":"1Chr","chapter":21,"verse":17,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נָ֤א","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTe"},{"reference":"1Chr 22 5","book":"1Chr","chapter":22,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נָּ֖א","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTj"},{"reference":"1Chr 29 20","book":"1Chr","chapter":29,"verse":20,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נָ֖א","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTe"},{"reference":"1Kgs 1 12","book":"1Kgs","chapter":1,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נָ֖א","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTe"},{"reference":"1Kgs 2 17","book":"1Kgs","chapter":2,"verse":17,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נָא֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTe"},{"reference":"1Kgs 8 26","book":"1Kgs","chapter":8,"verse":26,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נָא֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTe"},{"reference":"1Kgs 13 6","book":"1Kgs","chapter":13,"verse":6,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"נָ֞א","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTe"},{"reference":"1Kgs 14 2","book":"1Kgs","chapter":14,"ver